# Voyagely — Issue workflow (must follow)

When starting or finishing work tied to an Issue, follow this exact sequence.

## Start an Issue (before coding)

- **Merge previous work**: ensure the previous Issue is merged to `main` (or explicitly acknowledged as not needed).
- **Create GitHub Issue**: create/confirm the Issue exists on GitHub and capture its number (e.g. `#45`). Doc issue number (e.g. **#13**) ≠ GitHub number — always record both in `ISSUES.md`.
- **Create branch**: `feature/issue-XX-short-slug` (or `fix/...`, `chore/...`, etc. per `git-workflow.mdc`).
- **Update docs**: in `docs/issues/ISSUES.md`, set the Issue status to **🟡 IN PROGRESS** and note:
  - GitHub Issue number
  - branch name
  - (if applicable) previous PR merged

## During development

- Keep changes scoped to the current Issue.
- Ensure all interactive states exist: loading / empty / error / default / disabled.
- Keep i18n keys up to date for any new user-facing copy (at minimum **EN + FR**).

## Finish an Issue (agent executes end-to-end)

Unless the user explicitly says otherwise (e.g. “ne merge pas”), the agent **owns the full close-out**:

1. **PR**: open with `Fixes #<github-n>` in body; CI green.
2. **Merge**: `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch` (or squash per repo habit).
3. **Local `main`**: `git checkout main && git pull`.
4. **GitHub Issue**: confirm **CLOSED** (auto via `Fixes` or `gh issue close`).
5. **`docs/issues/ISSUES.md`**:
   - mark tasks + AC checkboxes
   - add merged PR link
   - set status **🟢 COMPLETED** (or **COMPLETED (MVP)** if post-MVP items remain)
   - update **IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTION** and **Progress Tracking**
   - check all **Finish (workflow)** boxes
6. **Commit doc** on `main` if the merge did not already include the final doc state: `docs(issues): mark #XX completed after PR #YY`.

Only then start the next Issue.

## Handoff — résumé pour changement de chat (obligatoire)

After each Issue completion, the agent **must** end the conversation with a **Handoff** block the user can paste into a new chat. Use this structure:

```markdown
## Handoff Voyagely — [doc Issue #XX] — [titre court]

### Livré
- [1–3 bullets : quoi, où dans l’app, PR/issue]

### Liens
- PR : https://github.com/igorms-pro/voyagely/pull/…
- GitHub : https://github.com/igorms-pro/voyagely/issues/…
- Branche : `main` (merged)

### Pas fait / reporté
- …

### Suite (voir `docs/issues/ISSUES.md` → IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTION)
1. …
2. …

### Brief pour prochaine conv
## Contexte
Repo voyagely, `main`. [Issue précédente] mergée (PR #…).

## Tâche
Issue #YY / [nom] — [une phrase objectif]

## Ne pas toucher
…
```

Pull **IMMEDIATE NEXT ACTION** and **CRITICAL PATH** from `ISSUES.md` — do not invent priorities.

## If the user says “on en a déjà”

- Do **not** recreate Issues/branches/PRs.
- Instead: verify current branch + local git status, then update `docs/issues/ISSUES.md` to reflect reality.
- Still produce a **Handoff** if the Issue is already done but the user is switching chats.
